use ../online/common

anchor("welcome", "### Welcome");

markdown "
natlang.online is an environment for building, evaluating, and sharing models
of natural language semantics. It's powered by nat, a programming language designed
to express ideas from the linguistic and philosophical literature on semantics in an
evaluable format.

<br>

To learn more about nat, consult the [language manual](/guide/natlang).
";

anchor("motivation", "### Motivation");

markdown "
Semanticists build formal models of meaning using tools from logic and type theory, but traditionally rely on paper or informal notation. Nat makes these models executable, allowing:

* Rigorous checking of analyses.
* Easier sharing and reproducibility.
* Integration of complex grammars across projects.
";